      narr:theme "factory-dame defaults to open-source / community-first monetization; commercial productization is a contingent path gated by external demand" ;
      skos:broader narr:StrategyOverview ;
      skos:note "The engine, voice primitives, and nd-* CLIs ship under a permissive license. Commercial paths (boxed hardware, hosted demos, SaaS) are held back unless unsolicited inbound from modular synth, jazz, or visual-art communities materializes. This posture is grounded in factory-dame's role as a creative counterweight to aswritten, where commercial pressure is explicitly excluded." .

    # ── Claims: Stance section ───────────────────────────────────
